Use `createMdxDocsSource` with any raw-file provider. The included `docsSource` uses an eager Vite glob for `src/content/docs/**/*.mdx` with English and French locales. A CMS or generated manifest can bypass MDX parsing with `createDocsSource({ pages, locales })` and records matching `DocsPageSchema`.

```text
src/content/docs/
├── en/
│   ├── introduction.mdx
│   └── operations.mdx
└── fr/
    ├── introduction.mdx
    └── operations.mdx
```

Every MDX file requires matching frontmatter and body titles. Localized versions share routing metadata while translating `title`, `description`, headings, and body content.

```mdx
---
slug: introduction
path: /docs
title: Introduction
description: Learn how to use the application.
icon: lucide:book-open
order: 1
locale: en
section: start
type: concept
legacySlugs: [overview]
---

# Introduction

Welcome to the documentation.

## First steps

Start here.
```

`section` is an arbitrary stable navigation group. `type` is one of `concept`, `tutorial`, `how-to`, `reference`, or `runbook`. `legacySlugs` is optional and redirects old public URLs to the canonical page.

